From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:23:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 430/443] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on 0429: resend
 after a rewind, say when the notice is withdrawn, lock the gate state, key
 the turn flag to the transcript

A rewind or fork fires no SessionStart, so the hook now records the transcript's line count and last message uuid at each full send and sends in full again when the transcript is shorter or no longer holds that uuid. When auto collaboration is switched off after a full send the model gets one "Omnigent notice withdrawn" line and the gate resets, so switching it back on sends the full block; the bridge now writes an empty context file when a message carries no notice, so a prompt typed into the pane is not mistaken for that. The auto paragraph keeps "routine work does not need a team". An Esc interrupt (no Stop) is read from the transcript's interrupt line, or from a full send older than 30 minutes, so it cannot block the every 20th prompt refresh. State is read, decided and written under an flock on a lock file in the bridge dir, failing open to a full send. The marker leaves out the preset clause when the notice names none. The golden test now checks a preserved baseline of the old wording, and both new test files run in upstream-smoke.
